##Steps I took to create and manage branches
To create a branch, I first went to GitHub and created a repository (repo). Then I launched git on my PC and cloned the repo. Next I entered the command:
>git checkout -b feature/footer
to create a new branch. I made my changes and committed the branch. To switch back to main, I checked it out.

##How I handled the merge conflict
When dealing with a mere conflict, I open the original file in Notepad++ and slowly go through the code and decide what to keep. Then I save and return to git to complete the merge process.

